<title>GREECE: CHASE MANHATTAN CUTS BASE LOAN, DEPO RATES.</title>
<headline>CHASE MANHATTAN CUTS BASE LOAN, DEPO RATES.</headline>
<dateline>ATHENS 1997-04-02</dateline>
<text>
<p>Chase Manhattan Bank said on Wednesday it is cutting its drachma short term base loan rate to 16.0 percent effective April 7.</p>
<p>The rate does not include tax surcharges.</p>
<p>Chase Manhattan's drachma savings rate will also drop to 9.0 percent, Vice-President Pantelis Kazanis said. --George Georgiopoulos, Athens Newsroom +301 3311812-4</p>
